    ('d6d56f24-f61d-505c-a9a5-348ab34dd678'::uuid, 'Henny Penny PFE 500', 'INSPECT CROSS ARM FOR CRACKS', 'Cracks in the cross arm are a major safety issue. If cracks are allowed to spread, the arm could snap while under pressure and potentially cause harm to team members. To inspect, detach the arm from the lid (CLICK HERE TO VIEW HOW TO VIDEO) and look for cracks, mainly in the section around the spindle.', 3),
    ('8f3a9c1c-b683-57b1-b0f4-cf3bfe68a9f9'::uuid, 'Henny Penny PFE 500', 'INSPECT UNIT FOR WORN OR MISSING PARTS', 'Look for anything that seems broken or worn. It is best to replace parts when they still have a little life left in them.', 4),
    ('7df41ece-7225-5f99-9bd8-6a0c5a597735'::uuid, 'Henny Penny PFE 500', 'INSPECT PUMP ASSEMBLY PARTS FOR WEAR OR BUILD-UP', 'There are two ways to inspect the pump assembly parts. The first is to remove the pump from the machine, disassemble the components and visually inspect the parts (CLICK HERE FOR VIDEO EXPLAINING THIS PROCESS). The second way is much easier but will not tell you as much. With the oil in the filter pan, disconnect the filter from the pick up tube and put your thumb on the pick up tube. Turn the switch to pump. If you have weak or no suction, then its a possibility you have bad pump parts and we recommend a visual inspection of the pump.', 5),
